Debith's direction (2026-09-12, trigger settled 2026-09-13): during work, memories record what was learned in that session, concretely and with the case. When the user asks to close the session — and only then — the agent reads back what it wrote and states once, at the level the cases support, a pattern several of them share. The design is overview §4.11, section 00a Feature 7, section 01 §4 and §8.

What was decided:
- The user starts a close, the way a commit is asked for. Nothing starts one automatically: the service learns a session ended only when its connection is gone, and a close nobody asked for would consolidate half-done work.
- A generalisation carries a `generalises` edge and retires nothing: its instances stay heads, as its evidence. A merge, by contrast, joins memories that say one thing and supersedes them.
- The service checks only what needs no prose: every generalised memory is a head, and the generalisation covers its instances on every hard dimension. `any` passes that check, so overreach is caught in review.
- Generalise only as far as the cases reach; a wider suspicion waits for a case in the wider space.

Still open (overview §10): whether a context spends budget on a generalisation's instances; what a later contradicting case should trigger. Not implemented: no `generalises` field on remember and no `review(session)` tool yet — until then, a generalisation cites its instances by key in its text.